# E-Commerce Data Warehouse Documentation Standards

## Python Module Documentation
- Every Python module MUST include a module-level docstring explaining its purpose
- Every class MUST have a docstring describing its functionality and responsibilities
- Every public function MUST have a docstring with:
  - Brief description of what the function does
  - Parameters section with types and descriptions
  - Returns section with type and description
  - Example usage when applicable
- Complex algorithms MUST include inline comments explaining the logic

## Airflow DAG Documentation
- Every DAG MUST include a docstring explaining the pipeline workflow
- DAG docstring MUST specify:
  - Purpose of the pipeline
  - Schedule interval
  - Dependencies between tasks
  - Expected data volumes
  - Error handling strategy
- Each task MUST have a docstring explaining its specific purpose
- Critical tasks MUST include comments about performance considerations

## SQL Query Documentation
- Every SQL file MUST include a header comment explaining the query's purpose
- Complex queries MUST include inline comments for:
  - Business logic explanations
  - Performance optimization notes
  - Data quality assumptions
- Views MUST document their intended use cases
- Stored procedures MUST include parameter descriptions and return values

## Configuration Documentation
- Configuration files MUST include comments explaining each setting
- Environment-specific configurations MUST be clearly marked
- Default values MUST be documented with their rationale
- Sensitive configurations MUST be marked appropriately

## Data Model Documentation
- Data warehouse schema MUST be documented with:
  - Table descriptions and purposes
  - Column definitions and data types
  - Primary and foreign key relationships
  - Partitioning strategies
  - Data quality rules
- Data lineage MUST be documented for critical tables
- Business definitions for key metrics MUST be included

## Pipeline Documentation
- ETL pipeline documentation MUST include:
  - Data flow diagrams
  - Processing steps and transformations
  - Data quality checks performed
  - Performance benchmarks
  - Monitoring and alerting setup
- Data generation scripts MUST document:
  - Data volume targets
  - Distribution patterns used
  - Skew and correlation assumptions
  - Validation rules applied

## README Maintenance
- README.md MUST be updated when:
  - New components are added
  - Architecture changes occur
  - Dependencies are updated
  - Performance characteristics change
- README MUST include:
  - Setup instructions
  - Running instructions
  - Troubleshooting guide
  - Performance expectations
  - Future enhancement plans